WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.877
How many of you honestly, 
when you're thinking&nbsp;about

00:00:01.877 --> 00:00:05.820
doing something vulnerable or 
saying something vulnerable think,

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.624
"God, vulnerability is weakness.
 This is weakness"

00:00:07.624 --> 00:00:10.335
How many of you&nbsp;think of vulnerability
 and weakness synonymously?

00:00:10.924 --> 00:00:12.000
The majority of people.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.357
And that myth is&nbsp;
profoundly dangerous.

00:00:16.357 --> 00:00:18.617
I define vulnerability as

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.507
emotional risk, exposure, 
uncertainty.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.514
It&nbsp;fuels our daily lives.

00:00:26.514 --> 00:00:29.646
And I've come to the belief -- this is 
my 12th year doing this research

00:00:30.379 --> 00:00:34.248
-- that vulnerability is our most accurate

00:00:34.753 --> 00:00:36.271
measurement of courage --

00:00:36.271 --> 00:00:39.701
to be vulnerable, to&nbsp;let ourselves
 be seen, to be honest.

00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:43.451
If we're going to find our
 way back to each other,

00:00:44.431 --> 00:00:47.381
vulnerability is going to be that path.

